From 1a67990f5accdbd7b88b4b4d7ae95fd582b0c15a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fred Chen <Fred.Chen@quantatw.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:09:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] i3c:i3c-hub: flush reg_work before configuring next port
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Commit 3f79dac3ea1c3 ("i3c: master: Defer new-device registration
out of DAA caller context") [1] moved i3c device registration out of
i3c_master_do_daa() into master->reg_work, run asynchronously on
master->wq.

i3c_hub_port_init_i3c_bridge() runs do_daa on the driving master
for each I3C port, then i3c_hub_port_init() immediately disconnects
the port and moves on to the next one. reg_work can still be
registering the device found on the current port when the port
mux is switched, racing against state it no longer matches and
crashing the kernel.

Flush reg_work right after do_daa so registration completes before
the port is disconnected and the next one is initialized.

[1] https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260608054312.10604-7-adrian.hunter@intel.com/

Uptream status:
We have notified the I3C hub vendor to submit the fix upstream as soon
as possible. However, they mentioned that additional use
cases—specifically idle-disconnect combined with hot-join scenarios—need
to be considered, and they are still investigating and running tests. In
the meantime, since this issue triggers a BMC kernel panic and breaks
the build, we are applying a local patch to unblock our work.
---
 drivers/i3c/i3c-hub.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/i3c/i3c-hub.c b/drivers/i3c/i3c-hub.c
index 8fbdc4e16..b30ea40b3 100644
--- a/drivers/i3c/i3c-hub.c
+++ b/drivers/i3c/i3c-hub.c
@@ -1571,6 +1571,8 @@ static int i3c_hub_port_init_i3c_bridge(struct i3c_hub *hub,
 	if (ret)
 		dev_warn(&hub->i3cdev->dev, "Failed to run DAA - port:%i\n", port->port_nr);
 
+	flush_work(&hub->driving_master->reg_work);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
-- 
